# The build context for `server/Dockerfile`, which is built from the repository root
# because the image serves the client that lives above server/. The COPYs name their paths
# explicitly, so nothing here is load-bearing for the image contents — the point is not
# shipping the rest of the repo to the daemon, and making a future `COPY . .` not silently
# drag the test harness and the git history into an image.

# Version control and this file's own history: the checkout is not the artifact.
.git
.gitignore

# CI runs from the checkout, not from the image.
.github

# The Node suites and the headless-browser checks. Nothing at runtime reads them, and
# inside the image they would sit in the served document root, downloadable at the
# same URLs as the game.
tools/

# Repo documentation, not site content.
README.md

# The server's local state and its test suite. Nothing at runtime reads them, and a local
# database must not be uploaded to the daemon — it is one `COPY . .` away from being baked
# into an image. server/ itself is NOT ignored, because the build needs server/index.js and
# server/lib/.
server/data
server/test

# macOS noise.
.DS_Store
